  "authorization": "User explicitly requested fixing the identified reader restoration defect, then committing and pushing.",
  "contract": "Within the available scroll range, repeated capture and restoration of an unchanged layout must preserve the reading offset and paragraph. After reflow, the paragraph remains authoritative when the old chapter ratio identifies a different paragraph.",
  "implementation": {
    "file": "apps/windows/src/views/Reader.vue",
    "coordinates": "Capture and restoration share the reading line at viewport top plus 100 CSS pixels. Client rectangles provide a viewport-relative scroll delta instead of offsetParent coordinates.",
    "selection": "Shared locate() selects the paragraph at the reading line, including preceding gaps and trailing space. Trailing chapter space retains the last paragraph.",
    "restoration": "Reuse the chapter ratio when it identifies the saved paragraph; otherwise place the reading line just inside that paragraph. A zero paragraph/zero ratio preserves the chapter heading. Fractional offsets are not rounded to integers.",
    "compatibility": "No storage schema, persisted fields, native command or book format changes."
  },
